      section: "CS",
      q: "A non-pipelined instruction execution unit operating at 2 GHz takes an average of 6 cycles to execute an instruction of program P. It is redesigned to operate on a 5-stage pipeline at 2 GHz, with ideal throughput of 1 instruction/cycle. In the execution of P, 20% instructions incur an average 2-cycle stall due to data hazards and 20% instructions incur an average 3-cycle stall due to control hazards. The speedup (rounded off to one decimal place) obtained by the pipelined design over the non-pipelined design is _________",
